            font-weight: bold;
            color: #b71c1c;
        }
        ul {
            list-style-type: none;
            padding-left: 0;
        }
        li {
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }
        table {
            width: 100%;
            border-collapse: collapse;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }
        th, td {
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            padding: 12px;
            text-align: left;
        }
        tr:nth-child(even) {
            background-color: #f2f2f2;
        }
        .cta-button {
            display: inline-block;
            background-color: #27ae60;
            color: white;
            padding: 15px 30px;
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: bold;
            border-radius: 5px;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <header>
        <h1>Proposal for Enhanced Accessible Infrastructure</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="proposal-summary">
        <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
            <strong>Project Overview</strong><br>
            A comprehensive study investigating strategies to improve the overall quality of life for individuals with physical, sensory, and cognitive impairments.
        </div>
    </div>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>1. Problem Statement</h2>
        <p>Currently, significant barriers limit the movement and participation of people with disabilities. This document outlines the findings regarding current infrastructure, policy gaps, and the necessity of targeted interventions.</p>

        <h2>2. Proposed Approach</h2>
        <p>We propose a model focusing on integrating technology and accessible design principles to bridge the digital divide and physical separation.</p>

        <blockquote>
            <strong>"Accessibility isn't just about physical doors; it's about connecting you to the best services available."</strong>
        </blockquote>
        <p>Based on the latest data, we aim to identify the highest priority areas where immediate resource allocation would most benefit marginalized populations.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h3>Research Focus Areas</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Navigational Technology:</strong> Evaluating screen reader compatibility and real-time translation tools.</li>
            <li><strong>Affordable Accommodation Plans:</strong> Assessing cost-effectiveness versus benefits.</li>
            <li><strong>Support Networks:</strong> Developing partnerships between local organizations and mental health professionals.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section" style="background-color: #e8f5e9;">
        <h3>Expected Impact</h3>
        <p>Upon completion of the research, we anticipate the following outcomes for all stakeholders:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Reduced costs associated with barriers</li>
            <li>Increased safety in public spaces</li>
            <li>Enhanced community inclusion rates</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The ultimate objective is to build a resilient society capable of supporting those who rely on our systems for their well-being.</p>
    </section>

    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2023 Initiative for Quality of Life Studies. All Rights Reserved.</p>
    </footer>

    <a href="#" class="cta-button">Download Full Report</a>
</body>
</html>
